# timerfd is virtualized against the deterministic clock: the host timerfd
# is a never-armed vessel and the blocking read completes at the guest's
# virtual deadline, not after host time passes. (This test was XFAIL while
# timerfd_settime armed a host-kernel timer; the virtual-time implementation
# turned it XPASS and the marker was removed, as that comment required.)
RUN: %hermit run --strict -- %me
